{
  "case": "23-box-owner-prefix",
  "description": "A rule-created agent inherits the longest common box path of its two parents (§2), so a host can answer 'which entity does this agent belong to' for a derived agent and not only for a survivor. Two players are boxed into one world. Inside `p1`, a `con` and a `dup` meet and commute — a firing wholly inside one character, which is the common case in a game — and every copy it creates is named `p1/_r<hex>`. `p2` reduces the same way and its copies are `p2/_r<hex>`: same rule, same shapes, different owners, no collision. `pin_ids` is what pins this; the canonical form is id-blind and would pass either way. The complementary half is case 24's: parents from different boxes share no path and get no prefix, because ambiguity is reported by saying nothing rather than resolved by guessing.",
